# Fixed 2026-10-03, defect 218, lane irverify.
# Symptom: a function of 400 `if` statements, one after another, took 55.71 s
# of user time to build on this Mac with the trunk's compiler at b7edbc35,
# and 800 were still building at 300 s; sampled at 200, the time was in the
# IR verifier's dominator fixpoint (`selfhost/ir/values.hero`).
# Cause: the fixpoint kept a row of every block for every block and went
# round them all until nothing moved, blocks squared a round, with no bound
# on the rounds but the blocks. The dominators are a Lengauer-Tarjan tree
# now (`selfhost/ir/dominators.hero`), and a read asks it in constant time.
# This case: 800 `if` statements, built and run.

function main()
    t: i64 @= 0

    if t == 0
        t @ t + 1

    if t == 1
        t @ t + 1

    if t == 2
        t @ t + 1

